WEBVTT

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:39.970
Robin.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.500
Robin?

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:44.800
You slept out here again?

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:50.040
Good morning...

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.380
Looks like you had another late night last night.

00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:57.490
Are you all right?

00:00:59.020 --> 00:00:59.720
Yeah.

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:02.690
You want some coffee, right?

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:10.660
Oh, right. Touko...

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:15.530
I saw you the other day. You were with Amon.

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:19.160
I didn't know you two knew each other.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.110
Are you a couple?

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:23.870
Hardly.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:33.910
Yes?

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:36.690
Amon?

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:37.660
Yes.

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:40.700
Right now?

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:44.890
All right.

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:58.440
I feel like it'll disappear...

00:01:58.270 --> 00:02:04.170
...the instant I look away.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:09.310
I just kept counting...

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:14.750
...all the many traces of loneliness...

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:22.120
...that I'd vomited up.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:28.060
In this time that seems so dry,

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:33.170
...my heart is thrashing around and drowning.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:39.030
It takes those lies that make my head spin...

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:42.080
...and tears them to pieces.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:51.750
 And the place I lose my way in...

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:59.580
...is a dim, hazy world.

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:24.700
You wouldn't normally see something crushed this badly from an impact or water pressure.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:29.030
Someone with extraordinary powers...

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:32.560
Assuming it was a Witch that did it.

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:35.800
The driver who died was Ryoji Kasai, age 32.

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:41.480
Do you remember the 200 million yen robbery that happened in Tokyo last month?

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:44.720
The one where they attacked a cash delivery truck?

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:47.880
One of the bills in Kasai's possession matched the number...

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:51.620
...of one of the bills taken from the delivery truck.

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:54.690
Plus, Kasai used to work for a cash delivery security company...

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:57.590
...up until three months before the incident.

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:00.500
In other words, he's almost certainly the culprit.

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:04.660
So what about it? We're going to find that 200 million yen?

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:07.100
That's under police jurisdiction.

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:13.680
At this time, the investigation for this case will be handled by the police.

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:17.890
We'll keep an eye on how the case progresses...

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.620
...as we follow the Witch angle.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:24.550
How have you been lately?

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:27.390
Life over here.

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:32.090
Well... It's like a race against the clock every single day.

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:35.800
I couldn't eat breakfast today...

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:40.480
That's pretty tough. You should take care of your health.

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:44.580
Could I interest you in another espresso?

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.010
Thank you.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:49.120
Yes?

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:55.720
The driver of the delivery truck that was assaulted was taken to this hospital.

00:04:56.660 --> 00:04:59.860
It's written in the police report, but we should verify it for ourselves.

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:04.160
Look, I've told you people again and again...

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:07.030
During the accident, the steering wheel went completely dead.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:10.330
Then you're saying it wasn't driver error?

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:11.910
That's right.

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:14.640
But why did you suddenly lose control?

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:19.810
How should I know? I had my hands full trying to save my own hide!

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:24.820
But a spot inspection of the car afterwards showed that the truck was fine.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:27.220
Which is why you guys suspect me, right?

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:30.780
You're saying that I was an accomplice and rolled the car over on purpose?

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:34.760
But that's not how it happened. I swear I didn't do it!

00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:39.200
I've had enough of this!

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:52.910
Come to papa!

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:00.990
I caught some police information.

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:05.460
Looks like one of the guys from Kasai's circle of friends has shown up.

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:08.000
Suneo Tazawa, age 37.

00:06:08.230 --> 00:06:10.430
He used to work for a scrap metal factory.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:12.560
Is he on the Witch list?

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:14.970
There were no hits from the list.

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:18.170
And the police?

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:20.480
They're already heading out to arrest him.

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:22.370
Shall we nab him ahead of them?

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:27.650
No. We can't intervene until we have hard evidence that Tazawa is a Witch.

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:30.850
Tell them to sit back and see how things progress.

00:06:31.150 --> 00:06:32.420
Yes, boss.

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:01.110
Mr. Tazawa.

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:19.230
Tazawa!

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:21.360
Dammit!

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:34.210
That's Tazawa!

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:38.450
Oh, no!

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:03.440
Michael, do you read me?

00:08:03.810 --> 00:08:04.640
Yeah?

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:08.140
Tazawa got away. The cops are in pursuit.

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:10.050
What about you guys, Miss Karasuma?

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:11.420
He got our car.

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:14.980
But there's no doubt that he's the Witch we're after.

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:17.920
I won't get caught!

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:22.020
Uncle, I'm thirsty.

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:24.530
Here, have some juice.

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:26.490
Thank you, Uncle.

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:41.510
The police cars went after him,

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:45.550
...but they lost sight of Tazawa's car around the Sasajima intersection.

00:08:45.890 --> 00:08:46.950
Sasajima?

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:48.820
And I did a little digging around.

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:52.620
The scrap metal factory that Tazawa used to work at is in that area.

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:54.320
You want to check it out?

00:08:54.730 --> 00:08:55.660
Where is it?

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:09.400
Sakaki, stop the press machine!

00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:21.540
How do I stop this?!

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:24.280
Sakaki, get clear!

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:41.530
Robin! Where are your glasses?!

00:10:42.140 --> 00:10:44.770
Oh. Sorry, I forgot.

00:10:45.070 --> 00:10:48.780
You know... What good is burning ME gonna do?

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:51.050
You have your Orbo, Sakaki. You won't burn.

00:10:51.050 --> 00:10:52.510
That's not the point!

00:10:52.750 --> 00:10:54.980
At times like this, you should have your glasses on beforehand.

00:10:54.980 --> 00:10:56.880
Sakaki! Call Michael!

00:10:55.280 --> 00:10:56.190
Didn't Karasuma...

00:10:57.220 --> 00:10:58.150
Send an ambulance!

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:02.120
There's a child inside the car.

00:11:02.630 --> 00:11:04.090
A child...

00:11:16.270 --> 00:11:19.070
It looks like he was given some drugged juice.

00:11:19.880 --> 00:11:23.830
He's fast asleep now, but it's nothing life-threatening.

00:11:25.850 --> 00:11:27.480
That's good to hear.

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:30.420
This is a pretty straightforward case.

00:11:30.420 --> 00:11:32.390
Tazawa is probably the mastermind.

00:11:32.860 --> 00:11:37.120
Kasai probably was reeled in for information concerning the cash delivery.

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:43.300
But the problem for us is the power that Tazawa used during the robbery.

00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:49.760
As all of you may know, many Witches try to hide their powers.

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:53.210
To have it manifest like this...

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:56.870
In most cases, this occurs when a sort of mental pressure or trauma...

00:11:57.180 --> 00:12:00.480
...throws off one's emotional balance.

00:12:00.850 --> 00:12:05.450
According to the police investigation, both of them had major gambling debts.

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:10.320
Which means this is a case of accomplices betraying each other for money?

00:12:10.630 --> 00:12:14.820
Or they both wanted the 200 million yen for themselves all along.

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:21.760
Either way, the only thing that's certain is that Tazawa has already opened Pandora's box.

00:12:22.670 --> 00:12:26.510
He'll no longer show any hesitation in using his powers.

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:28.580
What about that boy?

00:12:28.580 --> 00:12:30.310
Mamoru Kudo, age 7.

00:12:31.010 --> 00:12:33.070
He's a distant relative of Tazawa's.

00:12:33.720 --> 00:12:35.710
Apparently, his parents passed away recently,

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:39.410
...so for the past six months or so, he's been living with Tazawa.

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:43.190
Do you hurt anywhere?

00:12:46.260 --> 00:12:49.490
Okay, you're fine. There's nothing to worry about.

00:12:50.400 --> 00:12:54.730
Just to be safe, we'll keep you here for observation for two or three days.

00:12:55.940 --> 00:12:58.630
If you have a headache, call us right away.

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:05.140
Isn't that great? It's nothing serious.

00:13:05.550 --> 00:13:07.480
Hey, is there anything that you want?

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:09.680
Uncle...

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:11.850
Uncle...

00:13:12.820 --> 00:13:14.650
Where's my uncle?

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:16.780
Uncle Tazawa...

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:22.930
Mamoru...

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:31.670
He doesn't know that he was almost killed.

00:13:32.340 --> 00:13:34.370
He's so worried about Tazawa...

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:37.310
Well, he was acting as a replacement for his parents.

00:13:37.310 --> 00:13:38.440
And he still...

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:41.080
Honestly, that guy's like an oni.

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:43.850
Oni?

00:13:44.150 --> 00:13:47.920
For Europeans, I guess it's like like a troll or a goblin, maybe?

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:50.620
No, it's a little different...

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:52.520
A demon.

00:13:53.460 --> 00:13:55.190
A Witch?

00:14:08.310 --> 00:14:13.720
Like I said, we're just here to pick up that boy's clothes and personal effects!

00:14:13.720 --> 00:14:15.650
And to feed the parakeet.

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:18.650
If there's anything he needs, we'll send it over later.

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:20.750
In any case, crime scenes are off limits.

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:25.360
Not even the STN can come in without a proper warrant.

00:14:25.690 --> 00:14:29.490
The boy is in the hospital! Don't you understand?!

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:31.070
All I'm saying is...

00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:34.430
Well, wait. That much can't hurt.

00:14:34.770 --> 00:14:35.670
But...

00:14:36.710 --> 00:14:38.040
Wait there!

00:14:40.780 --> 00:14:44.270
It's just the rules. It's nothing personal.

00:14:45.180 --> 00:14:46.240
Sure...

00:14:49.020 --> 00:14:52.710
Here! This should be enough! Now hurry up and get out of here!

00:14:58.090 --> 00:14:58.960
Thanks.

00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:01.390
Dojima!

00:15:01.830 --> 00:15:04.660
What the hell is this "STN," anyway?

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:06.730
Forget about them.

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:10.840
I know lots of detectives who disappeared after poking their noses into that organization.

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:18.340
That really pisses me off!

00:15:19.110 --> 00:15:20.950
Did something happen?

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:25.150
Oh, that's Mamoru's parakeet.

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:27.350
You know Mamoru?

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:30.950
Oh, you two must be volunteers.

00:15:31.390 --> 00:15:33.950
You know, I feel so sorry for that poor boy...

00:15:34.230 --> 00:15:36.390
I heard that both his parents died,

00:15:36.730 --> 00:15:39.830
...and he'd been bounced around from one relative to another.

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:42.070
Bounced around...?

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:45.040
Yes, and?

00:15:45.610 --> 00:15:50.010
Well, Mr. Tazawa took custody, but all he did was neglect the boy.

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:53.570
It was just so pitiful...

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:56.610
But you know, he's a very strange child.

00:15:57.420 --> 00:15:58.940
Oh, there, there.

00:16:00.220 --> 00:16:03.990
You remember how they used to bend spoons on TV all the time?

00:16:04.390 --> 00:16:08.300
He did that in front of everyone. Turned it into a twisted mess.

00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:11.070
Maybe that's why all the relatives decided to stay away...

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:11.960
Wait a minute!

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:15.930
Mamoru was the one bending the spoon? Not Tazawa?!

00:16:16.310 --> 00:16:18.900
Tazawa? Now THAT's impossible!

00:16:19.270 --> 00:16:23.840
All that man can do is drink from dawn to dusk and make a ruckus.

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:27.650
About all he can bend is his elbow.

00:16:33.490 --> 00:16:37.550
I found it! There are signs of a Witch two degrees away from that boy!

00:16:38.190 --> 00:16:39.390
That settles it.

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:42.520
Then the reason Tazawa tried to kill the boy...

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:45.300
Was to get rid of his tool.

00:16:53.580 --> 00:16:54.410
Mamoru?

00:16:55.010 --> 00:16:57.270
The guys from the Factory are headed to the hospital.

00:16:57.880 --> 00:17:00.510
We need to take him into custody before the police make their move.

00:17:00.850 --> 00:17:02.650
But the Factory? That's...

00:17:02.990 --> 00:17:04.380
No personal emotions allowed.

00:17:04.850 --> 00:17:10.350
Tazawa may have been using him, but that boy has already killed one person.

00:17:32.710 --> 00:17:33.610
Can I help you?

00:17:34.050 --> 00:17:38.110
Um, about the patient in room 203... Is he being examined right now?

00:17:38.520 --> 00:17:40.550
No... Isn't he there?

00:17:40.790 --> 00:17:42.460
When was his last exam?

00:17:42.460 --> 00:17:44.790
I believe it was 20 minutes ago...

00:17:45.230 --> 00:17:46.750
Um, is something wrong?

00:17:47.930 --> 00:17:48.900
Hello?

00:18:41.780 --> 00:18:43.550
Damn! It's the police!

00:18:44.650 --> 00:18:45.810
Uncle...

00:18:48.360 --> 00:18:51.050
Uncle, it's me! Me!

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:54.020
M-Mamoru...

00:18:59.900 --> 00:19:01.990
Tazawa got caught in the police dragnet.

00:19:02.540 --> 00:19:04.510
Meet up with Amon and head over to the scene.

00:19:04.810 --> 00:19:05.770
They're at...

00:19:15.550 --> 00:19:16.590
Mamoru...

00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:18.880
He didn't do this to save Tazawa, did he?

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:20.120
Amon!

00:19:20.490 --> 00:19:24.080
Search the area! We need to find the child as soon as possible!

00:19:42.440 --> 00:19:44.670
Hurry up and pick those up!

00:19:46.950 --> 00:19:51.320
Uncle, did you try to kill me?

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:53.420
Who told you that nonsense...

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:54.860
You're not going to pick those up?

00:19:54.860 --> 00:19:55.690
Listen to me!

00:19:55.690 --> 00:19:56.880
Pick them up.

00:19:58.360 --> 00:20:02.360
Why? Tell me, was I in the way, Uncle?

00:20:02.360 --> 00:20:05.130
I-I'll give you the money. All of it, so just let me...

00:20:06.540 --> 00:20:07.800
You're strange, Uncle.

00:20:08.440 --> 00:20:10.230
This is my money.

00:20:10.910 --> 00:20:12.870
It was my power that got it.

00:20:13.740 --> 00:20:14.730
Right?

00:20:15.080 --> 00:20:17.980
But you and Uncle Kasai...

00:20:18.380 --> 00:20:20.940
You both try to hog my money for yourselves!

00:20:21.380 --> 00:20:23.280
F-Forgive me...!

00:20:23.790 --> 00:20:25.910
H-Help me!

00:20:40.540 --> 00:20:43.200
This is for trying to kill me.

00:20:43.610 --> 00:20:45.400
S-Stop...

00:20:46.610 --> 00:20:48.540
Stop it!

00:20:52.750 --> 00:20:54.150
Stop it, Mamoru!

00:20:55.980 --> 00:20:57.080
Stop!

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:14.390
But, but my uncle... He tried to kill me!

00:21:16.140 --> 00:21:20.160
I... Am I going to be locked up?

00:21:45.930 --> 00:21:46.760
It's all right.

00:21:47.340 --> 00:21:52.100
Even after all this, they'll forgive me because I'm a child.

00:21:53.010 --> 00:21:56.670
I'll be right back. I'm just a kid.

00:22:20.670 --> 00:22:22.530
The Factory, it's...

00:22:26.270 --> 00:22:27.370
Let's go.

00:22:36.770 --> 00:22:44.760
Just how far back do I need to go?

00:22:44.580 --> 00:22:47.620
Tell me.

00:22:48.830 --> 00:22:59.610
It's all so vivid that it hurts.

00:23:00.470 --> 00:23:09.500
The truth is, nothing can be shared,

00:23:09.180 --> 00:23:13.990
...so I never looked back.

00:23:15.260 --> 00:23:19.360
...all those promises...

00:23:21.300 --> 00:23:25.760
...inside me eventually...

00:23:25.050 --> 00:23:31.560
...gave up on that light from some other time,

00:23:30.760 --> 00:23:40.340
...like the light of a morning you can't return to.
